#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wave 41: Just Teens, a Third Time — the floor rises again.

Wave 40 closed by naming this wave as the next honest debt:
the 13/14 band was still the thinnest in the vault at 96
against 160 at the young end. This wave's fresh audit measured
the whole archive again before anything was built. Per-age
coverage at wave 40's close: 3: 160, 4: 160, 5: 329, 6: 426,
7: 496, 8: 530, 9: 524, 10: 518, 11: 456, 12: 446, 13: 96,
14: 96. Inside the band, the primary-category cells measure
seasons 6, outdoor 6, pe-movement 6, music-rhythm 6,
rainy-day 6, icebreakers 7, crafts 7, holidays 9, stem 9,
quiet-focus 15, team-community 19 — a floor of 6, shared by
five categories.

The wave's size is sized from those cells, the same way
waves 39 and 40 sized theirs: the eight thinnest cells in
the band are the five at the floor of 6, the two at 7, and
one of the two tied at 9. One record for each of those eight
cells is eight records — no more, no fewer. The tie at 9 is
broken on the tag shelves: the holidays record carries the
Lunar New Year tag, which stands at 6 overall — one of the
seven floor holiday tags — while no STEM tag shelf is
anywhere near as thin. Result, asserted in the wave log:
total 723 -> 731; age-13 coverage 96 -> 104 and age-14
coverage 96 -> 104, every other age unchanged; the 13/14
primary floor rises 6 -> 7 (every category in the band now
carries at least 7 primaries); 13-14-only records 20 -> 28;
and eight honest picks meet the build validator's 8-12
collection rule, so the 30th collection — "Just Teens, a
Third Time" — unlocks with no padding and no lowered bar.
The remaining gap to the 160 benchmark is 56 at each age,
stated numerically, not spun.

Deliberate neighbours, kept on purpose and named here:
- cold-stratification-seed-bank vs seed-library-opening-day
  (wave 39, a lending library whose packets carry tested
  germination figures) and seed-starting-cups (sowing in
  cups): the bank performs the COLD TREATMENT itself —
  seeds that refuse to grow until winter has passed through
  them, logged by chill weeks and proved by a spring test.
- transect-line-field-survey vs stream-watch-testing-round
  (wave 40, a stream read at fixed points) and
  bird-call-count (5-14, calls counted in silence): the
  transect reads DRY LAND on a fixed line — quadrats at set
  intervals, every species and surface recorded square by
  square, the line itself never moved between rounds.
- long-rope-turning-crew vs jump-rope-countdown (6-12, an
  individual personal-best counting game with a short rope):
  the long rope has TWO turners and a crew — turning is the
  skilled job, entry and exit are timed to a moving rope,
  and nobody jumps alone.
- part-singing-choir-first-rehearsals vs
  dream-speech-choral-reading (8-14, spoken text in chorus)
  and sing-it-back-echo-lines (echo singing by line): the
  choir sings in PARTS — two or more lines held at once,
  blended, conducted in rotation — singing, not speech.
- foley-radio-play-recording vs haunted-house-soundtrack
  (7-14, music and effects scored for a haunted house) and
  mini-podcast-studio (12-14, a spoken podcast): the play
  is a SCRIPTED DRAMA performed entire — actors, a director,
  and live sound effects made by hand at a Foley table,
  recorded in one take per scene.
- partner-portrait-interviews vs two-minute-mingle (8-14,
  many short chats against a clock) and hot-seat-kind-
  questions (wave 39, one seat, the group's questions): the
  portrait is ONE deep pair interview, note-kept, and its
  product is an introduction spoken by the interviewer —
  you present the person you actually met.
- one-sheet-zine-workshop vs origami-corner-bookmark
  (folding as a bookmark's craft) and comic-strip-creations
  (panels drawn in sequence): the zine is a whole folded
  PUBLICATION — eight pages from one sheet, laid out,
  sequenced, titled, and traded as finished objects.
- lunar-new-year-dumpling-folding-night vs
  red-envelope-wishes (wishes written for envelopes) and
  gelt-math-market (a market game): the night folds REAL
  dumplings for a real shared meal — teens fold, seal and
  count; the adult alone runs the steamer and the pot.

Two drafted records were cut before the pack ran, on the
standing near-dupe discipline: a pond-dip tray survey for
the outdoor slot — stream-watch-testing-round (wave 40)
already tips a net into trays and reads the citizens, and
still water does not make it a new record — and a New Year
letter capsule for the holidays slot — new-year-time-
capsule already seals the year's words away for later, and
older letter-writers do not change the ceremony. Both slots
were rebuilt from genuinely empty ground: no transect
record and no dumpling record existed anywhere on the shelf.

The drama/coding lane, recorded not padded (standing rule):
still no drama or coding category among the eleven, and no
validator tag names one. The Foley radio play is filed
under rainy-day, its honest primary; this wave does not
invent a twelfth category to look complete.

Safety notes are practical only — no medical claims anywhere.

Run once: dedupes by id, writes data/activities.json and
data/collections.json. Run scripts/build.py afterwards.
"""
